    "Held-out pitch harmonic-level error improves 10.994 to 5.871 dB and decay-slope error 3.805 to 2.499 dB/s, but all four pitch envelope errors regress; their mean rises 4.451 to 5.482 dB.",
    "Non-edge attack-rise error rises 9.134 to 19.268 ms. F#5v8 regresses in spectral, harmonic, fundamental and partial tuning metrics.",
    "Edge spectral/harmonic/decay errors worsen as a group despite improved tuning; the two edge samples are diagnostics, not evidence of validated full-keyboard extrapolation."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    {
      "kind": "model",
      "detail": "The radiation correction is a continuous-time steady-state observation approximation, retaining analytic phase. Broadband hammer/board transients are not uniquely identified; the attack regression must not be hidden."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ablation",
      "detail": "--no-sympathetic removes unstruck mechanical ports but radiationTransfer still sums their resistive loads. This optional ablation has an observation/load mismatch; the default all-string benchmark and demos are unaffected."
    },
    {
      "kind": "measurement",
      "detail": "One early-energy scalar is removed per case; amplitude velocity response is not validated by these spectral/envelope errors. Onset alignment and phase-insensitive powers also do not validate absolute latency, phase or spatial fidelity."
    },
    {
      "kind": "external_validity",
      "detail": "The 24 recordings share one Yamaha C5, microphone setup and library process. Physical hammer speeds, acquisition pedal state and precise release times are undocumented. No pedal/chord/polyphonic or blind perceptual validation follows from the isolated-note scores."
    },
    {
      "kind": "fit_provenance",
